export anchor NightTrailStyle:
    number: 390
    screen: FitnessTracker
    name: Night trail
    idea: A mountain trail at night seen by headlamp, with topographic contour lines in the dark, a warm beam lighting the run, heart zones stacked as altitude bands in a peak, the week drawn as a ridge, and goals marked by painted trail blazes.
    base: dark
    palette:
        night: #090e15, the page and the style sheet
        panel: #0f1823, cards, the hero and fields
        topo: #1c2a3b, contour lines in the hero
        line: #2b3d52, card edges, dashed rules and the climb path
        ink: #eef2f5, text and figures
        muted: #a9b7c7, labels, the ridge line, passed weeks and rest days
        beam: #ffe3a0, headlamp light, trail progress, today, zone 3, you are here, the primary button and focus
        blaze: #ff9a52, the move blaze, the next session sign and sheet markers
        onBlaze: #2a1204, text on blaze and beam
        moss: #9fd8a8, the exercise blaze and the Finished tag
        sky: #a9c8ff, the stand blaze and the tent
    type:
        One stack, Avenir Next, Avenir, Nunito Sans, Segoe UI, system-ui.
        The distance is 120px at 700 tracked minus 0.03em, hero stats 34px,
        sleep and goal figures 22 to 36px, the headline 22px at 600, card
        labels 13px caps tracked 0.14em, body 15px at 1.5.
    layout:
        A header with a peak and moon mark, Brightwork Move, Today, Week and
        Plan with an orange underline on Today, and Saturday 31 October
        after dark on the right. A full width hero card on dark slate with
        contour lines drawn on the right and a warm headlamp glow from the
        top left. It holds a headlamp glyph with Evening run in beam caps,
        the line Out and back under the headlamp, 8.2 km at 120px and a
        green Finished tag, and on the right Time, Avg pace and Avg heart
        rate over a rule. Below, a twelve column grid. Trail goals takes
        five columns, each ring a painted blaze, the name, value over goal,
        a dotted trail with a glowing beam fill and a dot at the percent,
        and a line with percent along and the amount to the goal. Heart rate
        zones takes seven columns with a peak cut into five horizontal
        bands, zone 1 at the base and zone 5 at the summit, each as thick as
        its minutes, zone 3 lit in beam colour, beside a list of zones with
        name and minutes. This week's ridge takes seven columns as a ridge
        line through the daily distances with dots and figures, hollow dots
        with rest on empty days, a flag on today and day names. A right
        column stacks Camp sleep with a tent, 7 h 12 min and deep 1 h 34
        min, and the Half marathon plan as a dashed climb of twelve markers,
        filled squares for passed weeks, a lit circle with you are here at
        week 6, hollow squares ahead and race week 12 at the top, then an
        orange arrow sign reading Next tomorrow Long run 14 km with View
        plan. Below 1000px cards stack. At 375px the ridge scrolls inside
        its card.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between cards, 22 to 24px card padding, 36 to 40px in the hero.
    density: Medium. A lit hero, then four cards that each draw one landscape.
    corners: 20px cards, 10px controls, 4px blazes and pills for tags.
    borders: 1px slate edges on cards and dashed rules between trail goals.
    shadows: None under cards. Light comes from the warm beam gradient and small glows on progress.
    icons:
        A headlamp, a peak mark, a tent and a flag. Goals use painted
        blazes, an orange circle for move, a green triangle for exercise and
        a blue square for stand. Passed plan weeks are filled squares,
        future ones hollow and the current one a lit circle. Rest days are
        hollow dots with the word rest.
    focus: A 2px beam coloured outline offset 3px with a soft 6px glow.
    tone: Outdoor and quiet, such as Trail goals, This week's ridge, Camp and you are here.
